WEBVTT

NOTE Cue timings are estimated from sentence length and pauses in the audio.

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.751
Welcome to the Concilium Security Risk Brief for Tuesday, November twenty fourth.

2
00:00:04.751 --> 00:00:12.391
Five minutes of security coverage from the last twenty four hours, to increase your situational awareness without decreasing your productivity.

3
00:00:12.391 --> 00:00:14.955
Here's what matters today.

4
00:00:14.955 --> 00:00:29.359
Today: a tighter British travel warning for parts of Ethiopia, a new Canadian warning for Riyadh's financial district, a car bomb in central Colombia, new U.S. sanctions on Iran's shadow banking networks, and a hospital hit during fighting in Mali.

5
00:00:29.359 --> 00:00:31.004
We start in Ethiopia.

6
00:00:31.004 --> 00:00:32.250
The U.K.

7
00:00:32.250 --> 00:00:38.156
Foreign Office now advises against all but essential travel to East Borena and Arsi, in the Oromia region.

8
00:00:38.156 --> 00:00:44.667
It continues to advise against all travel, or all but essential travel, to other parts of the country.

9
00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:45.894
Next, Saudi Arabia.

10
00:00:45.894 --> 00:00:55.017
Canada now says to avoid all travel to the King Abdullah Financial District in Riyadh, due to the risk of armed strikes, drone attacks and military debris.

11
00:00:55.017 --> 00:00:56.475
Turning to Colombia.

12
00:00:56.475 --> 00:01:04.952
Noticias RCN reports a car bomb attack in central Villavicencio, near the Meta department governor's office, injured twenty three people.

13
00:01:04.952 --> 00:01:11.098
Colombian media report heavy damage to the governor's office, homes and businesses, and no deaths.

14
00:01:11.098 --> 00:01:12.840
Next, sanctions.

15
00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:13.340
The U.S.

16
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:21.794
Treasury says it sanctioned more than two dozen Iranian exchange houses, front companies and key personnel to disrupt Iran's shadow banking networks.

17
00:01:21.794 --> 00:01:33.936
In a separate analysis, the Treasury's Financial Crimes Enforcement Network identified nearly fifteen billion dollars in financial activity since January 2025 potentially linked to Iranian shadow banking.

18
00:01:33.936 --> 00:01:35.040
And in Mali.

19
00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:43.545
On Saturday, November twenty first, a hospital in Niono, in the Ségou region, was hit during fighting, according to Doctors Without Borders.

20
00:01:43.545 --> 00:01:51.803
The group says two people were killed, including a health worker, and two other health workers, two caregivers and a child under five were wounded.

21
00:01:51.803 --> 00:01:53.944
Now a few quick notes by region.

22
00:01:53.944 --> 00:01:58.904
In Europe, Reuters reports schools across Germany and Denmark received bomb threats.

23
00:01:58.904 --> 00:02:07.968
In Ukraine, Reuters reports the regional governor says a Russian attack on Zaporizhzhia overnight killed two people and wounded forty, including four children.

24
00:02:07.968 --> 00:02:17.337
The U.N. humanitarian office says nearly thirty civilians were killed and two hundred forty injured across Ukraine between Friday and Monday morning.

25
00:02:17.337 --> 00:02:24.225
On cyber, Reuters reports a European Commission academy platform was disabled after a cyber attack, according to a spokesperson.

26
00:02:24.225 --> 00:02:37.412
The Record reports two Norwegian energy companies, including Equinor, were affected by a Microsoft cloud security vulnerability that hackers have exploited to target credentials, according to Norway's cybersecurity authorities.

27
00:02:37.412 --> 00:02:46.114
In the Middle East, Reuters reports Israeli strikes killed at least three people in Gaza, including a worker with the U.N.

28
00:02:46.114 --> 00:02:46.982
Palestinian refugee agency, UNRWA.

29
00:02:46.982 --> 00:02:59.406
Update on Iraq: the Institute for the Study of War says the government has not restored control over Jurf al Sakhr, where Kataib Hezbollah still has forces after a deal brokered by Iran's Revolutionary Guards.

30
00:02:59.406 --> 00:03:10.609
In Yemen, the Institute says the Saudi Air Force carried out airstrikes on Sunday, November twenty second, and Monday, likely to disrupt Houthi preparations for an offensive against Taiz city.

31
00:03:10.609 --> 00:03:19.460
In South Asia, Reuters reports former Bangladeshi Prime Minister Sheikh Hasina plans to return home from exile in India on December sixteenth, according to her spokesperson.

32
00:03:19.460 --> 00:03:21.322
In the Indian Ocean, the U.S.

33
00:03:21.322 --> 00:03:30.577
Geological Survey reports a preliminary magnitude six point four earthquake in the Mauritius and Réunion region early today.

34
00:03:30.577 --> 00:03:32.090
That's today's brief.

35
00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:40.295
These security developments come from government travel advisories and trusted analysts, curated by the Concilium Security Risk Management Team.

36
00:03:40.295 --> 00:03:48.463
The brief summarizes public reporting and isn't a substitute for your own risk assessment, so check the original source before making travel decisions.

37
00:03:48.463 --> 00:03:50.580
This brief is digitally narrated.

38
00:03:50.580 --> 00:03:51.511
Questions?

39
00:03:51.511 --> 00:03:54.907
Reach Concilium at info at concilium dot U.S.

40
00:03:54.907 --> 00:03:56.959
Thanks for listening, and stay safe.
